@* The connection, said in the top bar - and while it is down, a transparent overlay over the whole window that takes
   every click.

   While the connection is down the page cannot draw anything, so this is not drawn per state: Blazor's own script finds
   the element with id components-reconnect-modal and puts a class on it - components-reconnect-show (and -retrying,
   -paused) while it tries again, -failed / -rejected / -resume-failed when it has given up, -hide once it is back - and
   theme.css shows the text, the dot's colour and the overlay that class calls for. Each state's text is here already.

   The overlay because a click on a live page while its connection is down went nowhere: the button looked pressed and
   nothing happened, and nothing said so (an answer to a run's question, a cancel). Reload sits above it for when the
   script has given up - the page cannot come back by itself then. *@
<span id="components-reconnect-modal" class="conn" role="status">
    <span class="conn-dot"></span>
    <span class="conn-text conn-up">Connected</span>
    <span class="conn-text conn-retrying">Reconnecting…</span>
    <span class="conn-text conn-down">Disconnected</span>
    <button type="button" class="conn-reload" onclick="location.reload()">Reload</button>
    <span class="conn-block"></span>
</span>
